  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "DfygOxJxFLb8QcmgCnGeh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 165.39506700303582,
      "y": 269.2020847849269,
      "width": 1735.0987548828125,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bUq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1315250145,
      "version": 19,
      "versionNonce": 910757999,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779308949606,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| Event bus use case                                          | Why it matters in Swile-type fintech/benefits platform                                                     | Confidence |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| **State synchronization (wallets, balances, transactions)** | Critical: ensures consistency across countries, currencies, and services (card, app, payroll integrations) | 0.97       |\n| **Microservices communication**                             | Core backbone: decouples payments, benefits, merchants, HR, compliance per country                         | 0.96       |\n| **Error handling / compensation flows (sagas)**             | Essential for financial correctness (refunds, failed payments, reversals, retries)                         | 0.94       |\n| **Background job triggers**                                 | Settlement, reimbursement batching, FX conversion, accounting exports                                      | 0.93       |\n| **Logging & audit trail (compliance-grade)**                | Mandatory in fintech: trace every transaction for audit, fraud detection, legal compliance                 | 0.92       |\n| **Real-time notifications**                                 | Card payments, balance updates, rejection alerts, employer funding updates                                 | 0.90       |\n| **Analytics tracking**                                      | Product + financial behavior per country (usage, employer spend patterns)                                  | 0.88       |\n| **Plugin / country-specific extensions**                    | Needed for localization (tax rules, benefit rules, partners, legal constraints)                            | 0.86       |\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| Event bus use case                                          | Why it matters in Swile-type fintech/benefits platform                                                     | Confidence |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| **State synchronization (wallets, balances, transactions)** | Critical: ensures consistency across countries, currencies, and services (card, app, payroll integrations) | 0.97       |\n| **Microservices communication**                             | Core backbone: decouples payments, benefits, merchants, HR, compliance per country                         | 0.96       |\n| **Error handling / compensation flows (sagas)**             | Essential for financial correctness (refunds, failed payments, reversals, retries)                         | 0.94       |\n| **Background job triggers**                                 | Settlement, reimbursement batching, FX conversion, accounting exports                                      | 0.93       |\n| **Logging & audit trail (compliance-grade)**                | Mandatory in fintech: trace every transaction for audit, fraud detection, legal compliance                 | 0.92       |\n| **Real-time notifications**                                 | Card payments, balance updates, rejection alerts, employer funding updates                                 | 0.90       |\n| **Analytics tracking**                                      | Product + financial behavior per country (usage, employer spend patterns)                                  | 0.88       |\n| **Plugin / country-specific extensions**                    | Needed for localization (tax rules, benefit rules, partners, legal constraints)                            | 0.86       |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "r1iLSd0seDvBwczazSgxi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 525.9348619249108,
      "y": 742.8749999999995,
      "width": 1014.0191650390625,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bUr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 750304737,
      "version": 282,
      "versionNonce": 1657481871,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779308949606,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Here’s the **most common ordering in real system design usage (and interviews)**:\n\n1. **Asynchronous communication** → most fundamental reason event buses exist (remove blocking,\nimprove scalability)\n2. **Service decoupling** → core architectural benefit that enables independent teams/services to\nevolve\n3. **Event distribution (fan-out)** → natural consequence of pub/sub, widely used but slightly more\n“mechanical” than foundational\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Here’s the **most common ordering in real system design usage (and interviews)**:\n\n1. **Asynchronous communication** → most fundamental reason event buses exist (remove blocking, improve scalability)\n2. **Service decoupling** → core architectural benefit that enables independent teams/services to evolve\n3. **Event distribution (fan-out)** → natural consequence of pub/sub, widely used but slightly more “mechanical” than foundational\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
